From 54b6a978b64c5c1f9c99a9a82ed0e2e8e402d2e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Joan=20Bruguera=20Mic=C3=B3?= <joanbrugueram@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:29:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix build with Clang

We need to fix 3 issues:
- Clang seems to treat -Wstrict-prototypes more strictly than GCC,
  fix the actual root issue.
- For Clang, we can't use __GNUC__ to the check that the driver
  is built with the same compiler version as the kernel.
- Remove the -MD argument Clang complains about.
  As far as I can't tell, it doesn't serve any purpose anymore.
---
